  "body": "The part of the attribute getter algorithm [responsible for returning the backing OAEO](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#ref-for-dfn-observable-array-type%E2%91%A2) is only reachable for attributes whose target is an interface. However it doesn’t seem like anything forbids the regular attributes of namespaces from having ObservableArray as their type.\r\n\r\nIt seems like either:\r\n\r\n1. [the constraints for where ObservableArray is usable](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#ref-for-dfn-regular-attribute⑧) should say “...of interfaces” or\r\n2. [1.1.2.4 of create an attribute getter](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#dfn-attribute-getter) should be lifted up to be between 1.1.2 and 1.1.3.\r\n\r\n(Though I’m not sure which is what was intended.)\r\n\r\nEdit: seems like it probably should be the first, since the backing array is keyed by the target object. This would seem to imply a namespace member that exhibits branding, which seems undesirable.",
